        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">The smartphone has a processing unit, flash storage, RAM, and other connectivity features for standard Fairphone.\n\n# Included processes\nThe dataset for for Fairphone was taken from the life cycle inventory study of the thesis project of Güvendik, 2014, which analyzes the bill of materials and components of Fairphone 1st gen. It is acknowledged that the recent model of Fairphone 4 is currently sold in the market, yet the transparent inventory data is kept confidential in the LCA report of the company due to intellectual property. Therefore, the latter technical report was only used to validate the LCIA results of the cited literature. The weight of the smartphone is defined to be about 160 grams. The data for other bill of materials foraverage smartphones are mainly taken from the JRC technical report and other published articles. The modeled smartphone has a flash storage capacity of 16 GB and RAM capacity of 1 GB. According to the industry technology for IC smartphones, up to 6 stacked dies can be integrated in a single package to optimize density and performance. In the modeling, the area of wafer/die is assumed to be ~4 cm2 to represent total wafer logic area according to the literature.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
